From 166e84ff1f083021fa5200aba224f27ae7303c5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:04:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/57] hw/arm, hw/ssi, hw/misc: Button G, 7seg and Relay
 Clicks on the MC00 board

The MC00 board's Click table now describes a Click by mikroBUS signal
(RST, PWM, INT, CS on the header's pins 5/7/9/15 through a mikroBUS
Xplained Pro adapter): its device and bus (I2C on SERCOM2 or SPI on
SERCOM1), device outputs onto those pins, pins into device inputs, and
every pull resistor on the Click, from MikroElektronika's schematics.

New Clicks: buttong (a click-button driving INT, LED on PWM), 7seg (two
chained 74HC595 on SPI, LATCH on CS, MR# on RST, digits enabled by PWM)
and relay (relays on PWM and CS; no device). New parts: click-button
(pressed property) and 74hc595 (SSI shift register chain with latch and
master reset inputs, latched outputs as a QOM property).

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
