@@ -45,10 +45,13 @@ Click boards
 """"""""""""
 
 The machine options ``ext1=<click>`` and ``ext2=<click>`` plug a
-MikroElektronika Click board into the EXT1 or EXT2 header (as through a
-Curiosity Pro to mikroBUS adapter): I2C on SERCOM2 (PA12 SDA, PA13 SCL),
-INT on the header's pin 9 (PB02 on EXT1, PA28 on EXT2). The Click's device
-is ``/machine/ext1-click`` or ``/machine/ext2-click``.
+MikroElektronika Click board into the EXT1 or EXT2 header through a mikroBUS
+Xplained Pro adapter (DS50002671A): I2C on SERCOM2 (PA12 SDA, PA13 SCL), SPI
+on SERCOM1 (PA16 MISO, PA18 MOSI, PA19 SCK), and the mikroBUS RST, PWM, INT
+and CS signals on the header's pins 5, 7, 9 and 15 (EXT1: PA20, PB10, PB02,
+PA17; EXT2: PA10, PB22, PA28, PA15). A Click's device, if it has one, is
+``/machine/ext1-click`` or ``/machine/ext2-click``. The Clicks' pull
+resistors are modelled (from their schematics, v100).
 
 ``thermo8``
   Thermo 8 Click: an MCP9808 temperature sensor (``mchp-mcp9808``) at I2C
@@ -59,6 +62,24 @@ is ``/machine/ext1-click`` or ``/machine/ext2-click``.
   25000) sets the temperature, also at run time:
   ``qom-set /machine/ext1-click temperature 31500``.
 
+``buttong``
+  Button G Click: a pushbutton (``click-button``) driving INT high while
+  pressed, pulled low otherwise (R2/R3 10 kOhm); its LED is on PWM (on while
+  high). The QOM property ``pressed`` holds it down.
+
+``7seg``
+  7seg Click: two chained 74HC595 shift registers (``74hc595``, length 2) on
+  the SPI bus. LATCH (STCP) is CS, MR# is RST (4.7 kOhm pull-up), and PWM
+  switches both digits on (4.7 kOhm pull-ups: on while undriven). The first
+  byte of a transfer ends in the second register (the right digit); outputs
+  Q0..Q7 drive segments dp, b, a, c, d, e, f, g. The QOM property
+  ``outputs`` reads the latched outputs (left digit in bits 7:0).
+
+``relay``
+  Relay Click: relay 1 on PWM, relay 2 on CS, on while high; both pins are
+  pulled low by the driver transistors' base resistors. There is no device:
+  the relays follow the pads.
+
 .. code-block:: bash
 
   $ qemu-system-arm -M pic32cm-mc00-cpro,ext1=thermo8 -kernel thermo.elf       -display none -serial stdio
